      },
      "lineNbr": 43,
      "author": {
        "id": 3289503
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-05T07:00:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think it\u0027s necessary, as the manager class has the same lifecycle as the binder and also holds a reference to this context (AdapterService). Setting the manager to null serves as a means to prevent further calls on it and through the native interface - although it isn\u0027t quite correct yet due to threading.\n\nHopefully we\u0027ll get to a place where the binder threads don\u0027t reference the manager at all and we can get rid of the cleanup method completely - post onto the appropriate handler, which returns false if it\u0027s exiting although this will log a warning message. Or we can add an AtomicBoolean to more cleanly manage the state of the binder. What do you think?",
      "parentUuid": "c03dcf55_3abef28a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 43,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 43,
        "endChar": 25
      },
