        "id": 3289503
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-05T07:00:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is there a significant difference between doing requireNonNull vs allowing the null pointer exception to be generated? \n\nThe calls to these binder methods are coming from the framework code that we have control of, so it seems like checking non-null is added verbosity for not much gain.",
      "parentUuid": "abc9e474_4d47f770",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 69,
        "startChar": 26,
        "endLine": 69,
        "endChar": 43
      },
      "revId": "15974a1a9a20dca8aeb52227a10b3548a103019d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b50654e9_02318bc7",
        "filename": "android/app/src/com/android/bluetooth/gatt/AdvertiseBinder.java",
